# Cloudflare static-asset header rules.
#
# The whole dashboard is one 220KB index.html, so a stale copy of it means a
# stale ENTIRE app: after a deploy the site kept serving the previous version
# until the browser cache was cleared by hand.
#
# "no-cache" is not "no-store" — the browser may still store the file, it just
# has to revalidate before reusing it, and an unchanged file comes back as a
# 304 with no body. Cost is one conditional request per load, not a 220KB
# re-download.
#
# This lives in a _headers file rather than in worker.js because Cloudflare
# serves matching static assets straight from the edge without invoking the
# Worker at all, so a header set in the script never applies to them.

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
